  "ideographicDescription": "⿱夂口",
  "confidence": 93,
  "verificationStatus": "cross-verified",
  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "Walking 夂 and talking 口"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Pictograph of a foot (夂) entering an opening, (口), the opposite of 出 (exit). Based on the original meaning \"enter\", unrelated to the current meaning \"each\", which is a phonetic loan."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "異辭也。从口、夊。夊者，有行而止之，不相聽也。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 夂 (“sole of foot”) + 口 – to come, to enter; original form of 𢓜 and 格 (OC *klaːɡ, *kraːɡ). The mouth could be referred to the entrance of a cavern or building (see 高, 去 and 谷; however, this is not the case in 向). Compare 出.\nSino-Tibetan. Derived from 舉 (OC kaʔ) with distributive suffix -k. Cognate with Proto-Lolo-Burmese *ka (“all”) (Schuessler, 2007)"
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "異辭也。从口、夊。夊者，有行而止之，不相聽也。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "Different 辭. Composed of 口 'mouth' and 夊 'go slowly'. Each; Each; Not 相聽.",
